Version: 6.3.289, from Mozilla's release `pdfjs-6.3.289-legacy-dist.zip`: the legacy build, which
carries polyfills (core-js, below) for the JavaScript that the browser of an older VS Code lacks.
License: Apache-2.0 (the notice above); the license text is `media/viewer/LICENSE`.
Source: https://github.com/mozilla/pdf.js

The files are not modified, with three exceptions. The release is pruned: source maps, the
scripting sandbox, the debugger and the viewer's languages other than English are left out, and
`web/locale/locale.json`, its index of languages, lists only English. The four Liberation Sans
font files are replaced, see below. And in `web/viewer.mjs` the highest zoom, `MAX_SCALE`, is 10
(1000%) instead of 25 (2500%); the file says so in its first line, and `scripts/vendor-pdfjs.mjs`
makes the change. `media/viewer/vendored.json` records the versions, that change and the
SHA-256 of every file, and `node scripts/vendor-pdfjs.mjs --check` verifies them.

`media/viewer/lpdf-host.mjs`, `lpdf-toolbar.mjs`, `lpdf-pdfjs.mjs`, `lpdf-diff-zoom.mjs`,
`lpdf-diff-info.mjs` and `lpdf-theme.css` are Lpdf's own code and are covered by the MIT License of
this extension.

The release also contains parts under their own licenses. Each license text is in the
folder of the files it covers:

- `web/images/`: four icons (`altText_spinner.svg`, `annotation-paperclip.svg`,
  `annotation-pushpin.svg`, `toolbarButton-editorStamp.svg`) are MPL-2.0 and carry that notice
  in the file.
- `web/standard_fonts/`: the Foxit fonts are BSD-3-Clause (PDFium authors, `LICENSE_FOXIT`).
  The four Liberation Sans fonts are SIL Open Font License 1.1 (`LICENSE_LIBERATION`, with the
  copyright notice). They are version 2.1.5, unmodified, from the Liberation Fonts release
  `liberation-fonts-ttf-2.1.5.tar.gz`, and replace the 1.07.4 copies in the PDF.js release, which
  are under the GNU GPL v2 with font exceptions. They stand in for the Helvetica and Arial that
  Lpdf's PDFs name but do not embed, on systems that have no such font of their own.
  Source: https://github.com/liberationfonts/liberation-fonts
- `web/wasm/`: OpenJPEG (BSD-2-Clause), JBIG2 (BSD-3-Clause) and QCMS (MIT), with PDF.js's own
  bindings to them under their own notices (`LICENSE_OPENJPEG`, `LICENSE_JBIG2`,
  `LICENSE_QCMS`, `LICENSE_PDFJS_*`).
- `web/cmaps/`: Adobe CMap resources, BSD-3-Clause (`LICENSE`), for PDFs that use the predefined
  CJK encodings.
- `build/` and `web/viewer.mjs`: the legacy build has core-js 3.50.0 bundled into it, MIT, whose
